window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":19,"nomSourate":"Maryam","nomFr":"Marie","nomEn":"Mary","nomArabe":"مريم","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":44,"nbVersets":98,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ كهيعص","tradPropre":"Kâf, Hâ', Yâ', 'Aîn, Sâd.","tradEn":"Kāf, Hā, Yā, ʿAyn, Ṣād.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Kâf, Hâ,Ya, ‘Ayn, Şâd: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes.","explicationEn":"1. Kaf Ha Ya ‘Ayn Sad. The discussion on similar letters has already passed in Sūrah Al-Baqarah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-18-verset-110.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"ذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهُ زَكَرِيَّا","tradPropre":"C'est un récit de la miséricorde de ton Seigneur envers Son serviteur Zacharie.","tradEn":"[This is] a mention of the mercy of your Lord to His servant Zechariah","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cette sourate raconte comment ton Seigneur a fait bénéficier Son serviteur Zacharie de Sa miséricorde afin que cela te serve d’enseignement.","explicationEn":"2. This is mention of your Lord’s mercy on His servant (peace be upon him), which I relate to you to take lessons from.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ نِدَاءً خَفِيًّا","tradPropre":"Lorsqu'il invoqua son Seigneur d'une invocation secrète,","tradEn":"When he called to his Lord a private call [i.e., supplication].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Zacharie invoqua son Seigneur secrètement de manière à être plus susceptible d’être exaucé.","explicationEn":"3. When he called on his Lord quietly, so that it is more likely to be accepted.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّي وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّأْسُ شَيْبًا وَلَمْ أَكُنْ بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"et dit: «O mon Seigneur, mes os sont affaiblis et ma tête s'est enflammée de cheveux blancs. [Cependant], je n'ai jamais été malheureux [déçu] en te priant, ô mon Seigneur.","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, indeed my bones have weakened, and my head has filled with white, and never have I been in my supplication to You, my Lord, unhappy [i.e., disappointed].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il dit: Ô Seigneur, mes os se sont affaiblis et ma tête est couverte de cheveux blancs. Durant toute ma longue vie, je n’ai jamais été déçu après T’avoir invoqué. Au contraire, Tu m’as à chaque fois exaucé.","explicationEn":"4. He said: “My Lord, indeed my bones have become weak, the white hairs on my head have increased, and I was not unsuccessful in my supplicating You. In fact, every time I supplicated You, You accepted.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"وَإِنِّي خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِيَ مِنْ وَرَائِي وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِي مِنْ لَدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا","tradPropre":"Je crains [le comportement] de mes héritiers, après moi. Et ma propre femme est stérile. Accorde-moi, de Ta part, un descendant","tradEn":"And indeed, I fear the successors after me, and my wife has been barren, so give me from Yourself an heir","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"J’ai peur que mes proches ne se soucient pas des affaires de la religion en raison de leur préoccupation pour ce bas monde. Comme mon épouse est stérile, donne-moi descendant qui m’aidera à assumer la charge religieuse.","explicationEn":"5. And I feared that my relatives will not be able to fulfil the rights of the religion after my death, due to their engrossment in the worldly life. And my wife is barren, so grant me from Yourself a child to help me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"يَرِثُنِي وَيَرِثُ مِنْ آلِ يَعْقُوبَ  وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا","tradPropre":"qui hérite de moi et hérite de la famille de Jacob. Et fais qu'il te soit agréable, ô mon Seigneur».","tradEn":"Who will inherit me and inherit from the family of Jacob. And make him, my Lord, pleasing [to You].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce descendant héritera ainsi la Prophétie de moi et de la famille de Jacob. Fasse, ô mon Seigneur, qu’il soit agréé par Toi par sa pratique religieuse, son comportement et sa science.","explicationEn":"6. He will inherit prophethood from me and inherit from the family of Jacob (peace be upon him), and O Lord, make him pleasant in his religion, character and knowledge”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"يَا زَكَرِيَّا إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلَامٍ اسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ لَمْ نَجْعَلْ لَهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا","tradPropre":"«O Zacharie, Nous t'annonçons la bonne nouvelle d'un fils. Son nom sera Yahya [Jean]. Nous ne lui avons pas donné auparavant d'homonyme».","tradEn":"[He was told], \"O Zechariah, indeed We give you good tidings of a boy whose name will be John. We have not assigned to any before [this] name.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah exauça alors son invocation et lui fit cet appel: Nous te donnons une réponse qui te réjouira: tu auras un fils qui portera le nom de Yaħyâ, un nom que personne n’a porté avant lui.","explicationEn":"7. So Allah accepted his supplication and called out to him: “O Zechariah, I am informing you of what will please you. I have accepted your supplication and granted you a boy whose name will be John. I have not given this name to anyone before him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَكَانَتِ امْرَأَتِي عَاقِرًا وَقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et [Zacharie dit]: «O mon Seigneur, comment aurai-je un fils, quand ma femme est stérile et que je suis très avancé en vieillesse?»","tradEn":"He said, \"My Lord, how will I have a boy when my wife has been barren and I have reached extreme old age?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Etonné par l’extraordinaire pouvoir d’Allah, Zacharie demanda: Comment pourrais-je avoir un fils alors que mon épouse est stérile et que pour ma part, j’ai atteint un âge avancé et que mon corps s’est affaibli?","explicationEn":"8. Zechariah said, amazed at the power of Allah: “How will a child be born to me when my wife is barren and I have reached the limit of old age and weakness of bones?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"قَالَ كَذَالِكَ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ وَقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا","tradPropre":"[Allah] lui dit: «Ainsi sera-t-il! Ton Seigneur a dit: «Ceci m'est facile. Et avant cela, Je t'ai créé alors que tu n'étais rien».","tradEn":"[An angel] said, \"Thus [it will be]; your Lord says, 'It is easy for Me, for I created you before, while you were nothing.'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’ange qui lui rapportait les paroles d’Allah lui dit: Certes, ton épouse est incapable d’enfanter, tu as atteint un âge avancé et ton corps s’est considérablement affaibli mais ton Seigneur a dit: créer Yaħyâ d’une femme stérile et d’un homme en fin de vie est pour Moi chose facile. D’ailleurs, Je t’ai créé ô Zacharie auparavant à partir de rien.","explicationEn":"9. The angel said: “The matter is as you have said, namely that your wife is barren and that you have reached the limit of old age and weakness of bones. However, your Lord said: For your Lord to create John from a barren mother and a father who has reached the extreme old age is easy. And I created you before this, O Zechariah, whilst you were not something to be mentioned as you were non-existent”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِي آيَةً  قَالَ آيَتُكَ أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلَاثَ لَيَالٍ سَوِيًّا","tradPropre":"«O mon Seigneur, dit [Zacharie], accorde-moi un signe». «Ton signe, dit [Allah,] sera que tu ne pourras pas parler aux gens pendant trois nuits tout en étant bien portant.","tradEn":"[Zechariah] said, \"My Lord, make for me a sign.\" He said, \"Your sign is that you will not speak to the people for three nights, [being] sound.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Zacharie invoqua ensuite Allah en ces termes: Ô Seigneur, accorde-moi un signe qui me rassurera et m’indiquera la réalisation de la bonne nouvelle que m’ont annoncée les anges. Allah répondit: Le signe qui marquera la réalisation de ce que Je t’ai annoncé, est que tu ne pourras pas parler aux gens trois nuits durant, sans que cette incapacité ne soit imputée à un mal. Tu seras plutôt durant ces nuits bien portant comme d’habitude.","explicationEn":"10. Zechariah (peace be upon him) said: “My Lord, give me a sign I can feel content with and which will show that the glad tiding given to me by the angels has been attained”. He said: “Your sign of having attained what you were given glad tidings of is that you will not be able to speak to people for three days, not due to any illness, but rather you will be sound and well”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"فَخَرَجَ عَلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَأَوْحَىٰ إِلَيْهِمْ أَنْ سَبِّحُوا بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il sortit donc du sanctuaire vers son peuple; puis il leur fit signe de prier matin et soir.","tradEn":"So he came out to his people from the prayer chamber and signaled to them to exalt [Allāh] in the morning and afternoon.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Probablement le sanctuaire du Temple de Jérusalem.","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, Zacharie sortit de son sanctuaire à la rencontre des siens et leur fit signe, sans parler, de glorifier Allah matin et soir.","explicationEn":"11. Then Zechariah came out to his people from his place of prayer, and indicated to them without speaking to glorify Allah at the beginning and end of the day.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"يَا يَحْيَىٰ خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةٍ  وَآتَيْنَاهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"... «O Yahya, tiens fermement au Livre (la Thora)!» Nous lui donnâmes la sagesse alors qu'il était enfant,","tradEn":"[Allāh said], \"O John, take the Scripture [i.e., adhere to it] with determination.\" And We gave him judgement [while yet] a boy","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Il est sous-entendu que l’enfant promis, Jean le Baptiste, est né et a grandi.","explicationUnanime":"Yaħyâ naquit alors et lorsqu’il atteignit l’âge de raison, Nous lui dîmes: Ô Yaħyâ, prends la Torah avec sérieux et application. Nous avons donné à cet homme, dès sa plus tendre enfance, une bonne compréhension, une science étendue, du sérieux et de la détermination.","explicationEn":"12. Then John was born to him. Once he reached an age in which he could be addressed, I said to him: “O John, take the Torah firmly and with effort”. And I granted him understanding, knowledge, firmness, and resolve, whilst he was still a child.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَحَنَانًا مِنْ لَدُنَّا وَزَكَاةً  وَكَانَ تَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"ainsi que la tendresse de Notre part et la pureté. Il était pieux,","tradEn":"And affection from Us and purity, and he was fearing of Allāh","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En outre, Nous lui avons accordé une miséricorde venant de Nous et l’avons purifié des péchés. Il était pieux dans son observance aux commandements d’Allah et dans son renoncement à Ses interdits.","explicationEn":"13. And I granted him mercy from myself and kept him pure from sins. And he was pious, abiding by the commands of Allah and refraining from His prohibitions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا","tradPropre":"et dévoué envers ses père et mère; et ne fut ni violent ni désobéissant.","tradEn":"And dutiful to his parents, and he was not a disobedient tyrant.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il était bon, doux et bienfaisant envers ses parents. Il ne dédaignait pas obéir à son Seigneur ni à ses parents et ne désobéissait ni à son Seigneur ni à ses parents.","explicationEn":"14. And he was dutiful to his parents, soft with them and kind towards them. And he was neither arrogant regarding obedience to his Lord or his parents nor was he disobedient towards his Lord or his parents.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"وَسَلَامٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا","tradPropre":"Que la paix soit sur lui le jour où il naquit, le jour où il mourra, et le jour où il sera ressuscité vivant!","tradEn":"And peace be upon him the day he was born and the day he dies and the day he is raised alive.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que la paix et la sécurité d’Allah soit sur lui le jour où il est né, le jour où il quittera ce bas monde et le jour où il reviendra à la vie. Ce sont là les trois occasions où l’être humain ressent une détresse extrême et s’il les vit dans la sécurité et la paix, il n’y a rien à craindre pour le reste de sa vie.","explicationEn":"15. And peace and safety be on him from Allah on the day he was born, the day he shall die and leave this life, and on the day he shall be raised alive on the Day of Judgment. These three places are the most frightening a person goes through, so if he is safe in them, he shall not have any fear in any other place.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ مَرْيَمَ إِذِ انْتَبَذَتْ مِنْ أَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا","tradPropre":"Mentionne, dans le Livre (le Coran), Marie, quand elle se retira de sa famille en un lieu vers l'Orient.","tradEn":"And mention, [O Muḥammad], in the Book [the story of] Mary, when she withdrew from her family to a place toward the east.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rapporte ce que le Coran qui t’a été révélé, raconte au sujet de Marie lorsqu’elle s’éloigna des siens et s’isola dans un lieu situé à l’est d’eux.","explicationEn":"16. And mention, O Messenger, in the book revealed to you the story of Mary (peace be upon her), when she moved away from her family and stayed separately in a place to their east.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"فَاتَّخَذَتْ مِنْ دُونِهِمْ حِجَابًا فَأَرْسَلْنَا إِلَيْهَا رُوحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا","tradPropre":"Elle mit entre elle et eux un voile. Nous lui envoyâmes Notre Esprit (Gabriel), qui se présenta à elle sous la forme d'un homme parfait.","tradEn":"And she took, in seclusion from them, a screen. Then We sent to her Our Angel [i.e., Gabriel], and he represented himself to her as a well-proportioned man.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En plus de s’être éloignée d’eux, elle se dissimula à leur vue afin qu’ils ne la voient pas lorsqu’elle adore son Seigneur. Nous lui envoyâmes alors Gabriel qui se présenta à elle sous l’apparence d’un homme bien proportionné et elle craignit qu’il lui veuille du mal.","explicationEn":"17. Thus, she made for herself a veil from the people which would cover her, so that they cannot see her when she is worshipping her Lord. Then I sent Gabriel (peace be upon him) to her, thus he appeared to her in the form of a perfectly-formed human. So she thought he has a malicious intention towards her.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"قَالَتْ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِالرَّحْمَانِ مِنْكَ إِنْ كُنْتَ تَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"Elle dit: «Je me réfugie contre toi auprès du Tout Miséricordieux. Si tu es pieux, [ne m'approche point].»","tradEn":"She said, \"Indeed, I seek refuge in the Most Merciful from you, [so leave me], if you should be fearing of Allāh.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Voyant cet homme bien proportionné se diriger vers elle, elle dit: Je me réfugie auprès du Tout Miséricordieux contre tout mal qui pourrait provenir de toi, si tu es pieux et que tu crains Allah.","explicationEn":"18. So when she saw him in the form of a perfectly-formed human heading towards her, she said: “I seek protection of the Merciful from you that any harm should come to me from you, if you are pious and fear Allah”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"قَالَ إِنَّمَا أَنَا رَسُولُ رَبِّكِ لِأَهَبَ لَكِ غُلَامًا زَكِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Je suis en fait un Messager de ton Seigneur pour te faire don d'un fils pur».","tradEn":"He said, \"I am only the messenger of your Lord to give you [news of] a pure boy [i.e., son].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Gabriel répondit: Je ne suis pas un être humain mais plutôt un messager que ton Seigneur a envoyé afin de te donner un fils bon et pur.","explicationEn":"19. Gabriel (peace be upon him) said: “I am not a human. I am only a Messenger from your Lord who He has sent to you for me to give you a good pure child”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"قَالَتْ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِي بَشَرٌ وَلَمْ أَكُ بَغِيًّا","tradPropre":"Elle dit: «Comment aurais-je un fils, quand aucun homme ne m'a touchée, et que je ne suis pas prostituée?»","tradEn":"She said, \"How can I have a boy while no man has touched me and I have not been unchaste?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Etonnée, Marie s’exclama: Comment pourrais-je avoir un fils alors que je n’ai pas d’époux et que je ne pratique pas la fornication?","explicationEn":"20. Mary said surprisingly: “How can I have a child when neither a husband nor anyone else has come near me nor am I an adulteress that I should have a child?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"قَالَ كَذَالِكِ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَيَّ هَيِّنٌ  وَلِنَجْعَلَهُ آيَةً لِلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِنَّا  وَكَانَ أَمْرًا مَقْضِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Ainsi sera-t-il! Cela M'est facile, a dit ton Seigneur! Et Nous ferons de lui un signe pour les gens, et une miséricorde de Notre part. C'est une affaire déjà décidée».","tradEn":"He said, \"Thus [it will be]; your Lord says, 'It is easy for Me, and We will make him a sign to the people and a mercy from Us. And it is a matter [already] decreed.'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Gabriel lui répondit: Même si aucun homme ne t’a approchée, ni dans le cadre du mariage ni dans une relation illicite, ton Seigneur dit: Créer un enfant sans père M’est chose facile. Nous mettrons dans le garçon que tu auras, un signe du pouvoir d’Allah adressé aux gens et Nous ferons de lui une miséricorde de Notre part pour toi et pour ceux qui croient en lui. La création de ton fils est une décision déjà prise et consignée dans la Table Préservée.","explicationEn":"21. Gabriel said to her: “The matter is as you said, namely that no husband or anyone else has touched you nor are you an adulteress. However, your Lord said: ‘To create a child without a father is easy for Me. And it is so that the child granted to you is a sign for people of the power of Allah, and a mercy from Me to them, due to the good they will achieve through him. And the creation of this child of yours is a fixed decree from Allah and written in the Preserved Tablet’.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"۞ فَحَمَلَتْهُ فَانْتَبَذَتْ بِهِ مَكَانًا قَصِيًّا","tradPropre":"Elle devint donc enceinte [de l'enfant], et elle se retira avec lui en un lieu éloigné.","tradEn":"So she conceived him, and she withdrew with him to a remote place.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> L’ange Gabriel, dit-on, souffla dans le col de l’habit qu’elle portait. Le souffle descendit alors à travers le vêtement jusqu’à atteindre sa matrice. Par la volonté d’Allah, elle tomba enceinte de Jésus.","explicationUnanime":"Après que l’ange ait insufflé en elle, elle devint enceinte et se retira loin des gens.","explicationEn":"22. So she conceived him after the angel blew into her, then she withdrew with him to a place far from the people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"فَأَجَاءَهَا الْمَخَاضُ إِلَىٰ جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ قَالَتْ يَا لَيْتَنِي مِتُّ قَبْلَ هَاذَا وَكُنْتُ نَسْيًا مَنْسِيًّا","tradPropre":"Puis les douleurs de l'enfantement l'amenèrent au tronc du palmier, et elle dit: «Malheur à moi! Que je fusse morte avant cet instant! Et que je fusse totalement oubliée!»","tradEn":"And the pains of childbirth drove her to the trunk of a palm tree. She said, \"Oh, I wish I had died before this and was in oblivion, forgotten.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est au pied d’un palmier que les douleurs de l’accouchement la surprirent. Marie dit: Si seulement la mort m’avait soustraite à ce monde bien avant ce jour. On m’aurait alors totalement oubliée et on ne m’aurait pas reproché cet enfantement suspect.","explicationEn":"23. And the pangs of childbirth struck her and made her take refuge by the trunk of a date tree. Mary said: “If only I had died before this day and I was something not even mentioned, so that bad is not thought of me”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"فَنَادَاهَا مِنْ تَحْتِهَا أَلَّا تَحْزَنِي قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا","tradPropre":"Alors, il l'appela d'au-dessous d'elle, [lui disant:] «Ne t'afflige pas. Ton Seigneur a placé à tes pieds une source.","tradEn":"But he called her from below her, \"Do not grieve; your Lord has provided beneath you a stream.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Celle de l’enfant Jésus, selon certains exégètes, ou de Gabriel, selon d’autres.","explicationUnanime":"D’en-dessous d’elle, Jésus lui dit: Ne sois pas triste. Ton Seigneur a fait couler à tes pieds un ruisseau où tu peux t’abreuver.","explicationEn":"24. Then Gabriel called to her from the bottom of the valley: “Do not grieve. Your Lord has made for you a spring of water beneath you from which you can drink.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"وَهُزِّي إِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسَاقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا","tradPropre":"Secoue vers toi le tronc du palmier: il fera tomber sur toi des dattes fraîches et mûres.","tradEn":"And shake toward you the trunk of the palm tree; it will drop upon you ripe, fresh dates.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ajouta: Pour te nourrir, secoue le tronc du palmier et alors, des dattes mures et fraîche tomberont près de toi.","explicationEn":"25. And hold the trunk of the tree and shake it; it will instantly drop fresh ripe dates on you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"فَكُلِي وَاشْرَبِي وَقَرِّي عَيْنًا  فَإِمَّا تَرَيِنَّ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ أَحَدًا فَقُولِي إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمَانِ صَوْمًا فَلَنْ أُكَلِّمَ الْيَوْمَ إِنْسِيًّا","tradPropre":"Mange donc et bois et que ton œil se réjouisse! Si tu vois quelqu'un d'entre les humains, dis [lui:] «Assurément, j'ai voué un jeûne au Tout Miséricordieux: je ne parlerai donc aujourd'hui à aucun être humain».","tradEn":"So eat and drink and be contented. And if you see from among humanity anyone, say, 'Indeed, I have vowed to the Most Merciful abstention, so I will not speak today to [any] man.'\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Après cela. Autre traduction : si tu rencontres quelqu’un, fais-lui comprendre par un signe que, ayant fait vœu de silence au Tout Miséricordieux, tu n’adresseras aujourd’hui la parole à personne.","explicationUnanime":"Mange les dattes que tu as cueillies, bois de l’eau du ruisseau, réjouis-toi de la naissance de ton fils et n’éprouve pas de tristesse. Si tu rencontres quelqu’un et qu’il te questionne au sujet du nouveau-né, fais-lui comprendre: J’ai pris l’engagement devant Allah de rester silencieuse aujourd’hui. Je ne parlerai donc à personne.","explicationEn":"26. So eat of the ripe dates, drink of the water, and be pleased with your child and do not grieve. And if you see any person who asks you regarding the child, say to him: ‘I have bound myself to silence for my Lord’s sake, so I will not speak to any person today’”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"فَأَتَتْ بِهِ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهُ  قَالُوا يَا مَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا","tradPropre":"Puis elle vint auprès des siens en le portant [le bébé]. Ils dirent: «O Marie, tu as fait une chose monstrueuse!","tradEn":"Then she brought him to her people, carrying him. They said, \"O Mary, you have certainly done a thing unprecedented.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Elle se rendit ensuite auprès des siens en portant son fils. Leur réprobation leur fit dire: Ô Marie, tu as commis une faute affreuse en mettant au monde un enfant alors que tu n’es pas mariée.","explicationEn":"27. Then Mary came carrying her child to her people. Her people said to her out of shock: “O Mary, you have committed a grave fabricated matter, by bringing a child without a father.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"يَا أُخْتَ هَارُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوكِ امْرَأَ سَوْءٍ وَمَا كَانَتْ أُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا","tradPropre":"«Sœur de Hârûn, ton père n'était pas un homme de mal et ta mère n'était pas une prostituée».","tradEn":"O sister [i.e., descendant] of Aaron, your father was not a man of evil, nor was your mother unchaste.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô toi qui ressemble à Aaron –un homme pieux– de par ton adoration assidue, ton père ne pratiquait pas la fornication et ta mère non plus. Tu es en effet issue d’un foyer pur et vertueux. Comment as-tu pu te rendre coupable d’une telle faute?","explicationEn":"28. O one who resembles Aaron (a righteous man) in worship, your father was not an adulterer nor was your mother. You are from a pure household known to be righteous, so how can you bring a child without a father?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"فَأَشَارَتْ إِلَيْهِ  قَالُوا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَنْ كَانَ فِي الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Elle fit alors un signe vers lui [le bébé]. Ils dirent: «Comment parlerions-nous à un bébé au berceau?»","tradEn":"So she pointed to him. They said, \"How can we speak to one who is in the cradle a child?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Elle fit alors signe à son fils Jésus qui était dans un berceau mais les siens la questionnèrent, étonnés: Comment un bébé dans son berceau nous comprendrait-il?","explicationEn":"29. She pointed towards her son Jesus (peace be upon him) who was in the cradle. So the people said in surprise: “How can we talk to a child who is in the cradle?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"قَالَ إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ آتَانِيَ الْكِتَابَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Mais (le bébé) dit: «Je suis vraiment le serviteur d'Allah. Il m'a donné le Livre et m'a désigné Prophète.","tradEn":"[Jesus] said, \"Indeed, I am the servant of Allāh. He has given me the Scripture and made me a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est alors que Jésus dit: Je suis le serviteur d’Allah qui m’a révélé l’Evangile et a fait de moi l’un de Ses prophètes.","explicationEn":"30. Jesus (peace be upon him) said: “I am the servant of Allah. He gave me the Gospel and made me one of His prophets.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُ وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا","tradPropre":"Où que je sois, Il m'a rendu béni; et Il m'a recommandé, tant que je vivrai, la prière et la Zakât;","tradEn":"And He has made me blessed wherever I am and has enjoined upon me prayer and zakāh as long as I remain alive","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il a fait en sorte que je sois bénéfique aux gens où que je sois et m’a ordonné d’accomplir la prière, de m’acquitter de l’aumône légale tant que je serai en vie.","explicationEn":"31. And He made me a great benefit for the servants wherever I am. And He ordered me to perform prayer and give Zakat for as long as I live.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"وَبَرًّا بِوَالِدَتِي وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِي جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"et la bonté envers ma mère. Il ne m'a fait ni violent ni malheureux.","tradEn":"And [made me] dutiful to my mother, and He has not made me a wretched tyrant.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il a aussi fait de moi quelqu’un de bon envers ma mère et quelqu’un qui ne dédaigne pas Lui obéir.","explicationEn":"32. And He made me righteous to my mother. And He did not make me arrogant towards the obedience of my Lord nor did He make me disobedient to her.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدْتُ وَيَوْمَ أَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ أُبْعَثُ حَيًّا","tradPropre":"Et que la paix soit sur moi le jour où je naquis, le jour où je mourrai, et le jour où je serai ressuscité vivant.»","tradEn":"And peace is on me the day I was born and the day I will die and the day I am raised alive.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que je sois préservé de Satan et de ses aides le jour de ma naissance, le jour de ma mort et le jour où je serai ressuscité afin qu’aucun mal ne m’atteigne durant ces jours les plus graves de mon existence.","explicationEn":"33. And safety from the satans and his helpers is on me on the day of my birth, the day of my death and the day I shall be raised on the Day of Judgment. The satan has no evil effect on me in these three frightening places”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"ذَالِكَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ  قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِي فِيهِ يَمْتَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Tel est Issa (Jésus), fils de Marie: parole de vérité, dont ils doutent.","tradEn":"That is Jesus, the son of Mary - the word of truth about which they are in dispute.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’homme décrit ici est Jésus fils de Marie (‘îsâ bnu maryama) et la description qui est faite de lui est véridique, contrairement à celle des égarés qui en détiennent des versions douteuses et contradictoires.","explicationEn":"34. He who is described with these qualities is Jesus, son of Mary. And this discussion is the word of truth regarding him, not that which is said by the misguided who doubt and disagree in his affair.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"مَا كَانَ لِلَّهِ أَنْ يَتَّخِذَ مِنْ وَلَدٍ  سُبْحَانَهُ  إِذَا قَضَىٰ أَمْرًا فَإِنَّمَا يَقُولُ لَهُ كُنْ فَيَكُونُ","tradPropre":"Il ne convient pas à Allah de S'attribuer un fils. Gloire et Pureté à Lui! Quand Il décide d'une chose, Il dit seulement: «Sois!» et elle est.","tradEn":"It is not [befitting] for Allāh to take a son; exalted is He! When He decrees an affair, He only says to it, \"Be,\" and it is.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ne convient pas qu’Allah ait un fils, que cela soit exclus en ce qui Le concerne et qu’Il soit sanctifié! Lorsqu’Il veut quelque chose, Il Lui suffit de dire « Kun (sois) » et alors ce qu’Il veut se met incontestablement à exister. Il est donc exclu que Celui qui détient ce pouvoir ait un fils.","explicationEn":"35. It does not befit Allah to have a son, exalted and free He is from this. When He intends something, it is enough for Him to say regarding this thing: Be, and it most definitely becomes. So He who is like this is free from having a son.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ اللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوهُ  هَاذَا صِرَاطٌ مُسْتَقِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Certes, Allah est mon Seigneur tout comme votre Seigneur. Adorez-le donc. Voilà un droit chemin».","tradEn":"[Jesus said], \"And indeed, Allāh is my Lord and your Lord, so worship Him. That is a straight path.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah, exalté soit-Il, est mon Seigneur et le vôtre. Adorez-Le donc exclusivement. Ceci est le droit chemin qui conduit vers l’agrément d’Allah.","explicationEn":"36. And Allah, may He be glorified, is both my Lord and your Lord, so make worship sincere for Him alone. This which I have mentioned to you is the straight path that leads to the pleasure of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"فَاخْتَلَفَ الْأَحْزَابُ مِنْ بَيْنِهِمْ  فَوَيْلٌ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ مَشْهَدِ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ","tradPropre":"[par la suite,] les sectes divergèrent entre elles. Alors, malheur aux mécréants lors de la vue d'un jour terrible!","tradEn":"Then the factions differed [concerning Jesus] from among them, so woe to those who disbelieved - from the scene of a tremendous Day.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Chrétiennes, précisent certains exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"C’est plus tard que les gens de la communauté de Jésus divergèrent à son sujet. Certains crurent en lui et le qualifièrent de messager, d’autres mécrurent en lui comme les juifs, enfin d’autres firent preuve de fanatisme à son égard. Une faction parmi ces derniers prétendit qu’il est Allah et une autre le considéra comme le fils d’Allah, qu’Allah soit élevé au-dessus de ces allégations. Malheur à ceux qui divergent à son sujet: ils vivront des scènes terribles le Jour de la Résurrection durant lequel ils rendront des comptes et seront punis.","explicationEn":"37. But the factions of Jews and Christians differed regarding the matter of Jesus (peace be upon him). The Jews said about him that he is a magician. Some Christians said about him that he is the son of Allah. Woe to those who differ regarding him, from witnessing the great Day of Judgment, due to its scenes, reckoning and punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"أَسْمِعْ بِهِمْ وَأَبْصِرْ يَوْمَ يَأْتُونَنَا  لَاكِنِ الظَّالِمُونَ الْيَوْمَ فِي ضَلَالٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Comme ils entendront et verront bien le jour où ils viendront à Nous! Mais aujourd'hui, les injustes sont dans un égarement évident.","tradEn":"How [clearly] they will hear and see the Day they come to Us, but the wrongdoers today are in clear error.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Leur ouïe et leur vue seront opérationnelles ce jour-là mais elles leur seront inutiles. Ceux qui sont injustes dans ce bas monde s’égarent de manière manifeste du droit chemin et ne se préparent pas à l’au-delà. Ils sont alors surpris par la mort dans cet état d’injustice.","explicationEn":"38. How horrible is what they will hear and see on the Day of Judgment, and how severe it will be for them. And how strange will be their condition which you will see. However, the oppressors in this worldly life are clearly misguided from the straight path. They will not prepare for the afterlife until it will suddenly come to them whilst they are in their wrongdoing.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"وَأَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ إِذْ قُضِيَ الْأَمْرُ وَهُمْ فِي غَفْلَةٍ وَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Et avertis-les du jour du Regret, quand tout sera réglé; alors qu'ils sont [dans ce monde] inattentifs et qu'ils ne croient pas.","tradEn":"And warn them, [O Muḥammad], of the Day of Regret, when the matter will be concluded; and [yet], they are in [a state of] heedlessness, and they do not believe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, avertis les gens contre le Jour du Regret lorsque les malfaisants regretteront leur malfaisance, et que les bienfaisants regretteront ne pas avoir accompli plus de bonnes œuvres. Ce jour-là, les registres des serviteurs seront pliés. Ils auront terminé de rendre des comptes et chacun ira là où l’auront conduit ses œuvres. Malgré cela, ils sont trompés par la vie ici-bas qui les distrait de l’au-delà et ils ne croient pas au Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"39. And warn the people, O Messenger, of the Day of Regret when the evildoer will regret his evil-doings and when the righteous will regret not being more obedient, when the scrolls of the servants will be wrapped, their reckoning is finished and each person goes towards what he had sent forward. But they have been deceived by their worldly life and are unmindful of the Hearafter, and they do not accept the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَرِثُ الْأَرْضَ وَمَنْ عَلَيْهَا وَإِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُونَ","tradPropre":"C'est Nous, en vérité, qui hériterons la terre et tout ce qui s'y trouve, et c'est à Nous qu'ils seront ramenés.","tradEn":"Indeed, it is We who will inherit the earth and whoever is on it, and to Us they will be returned.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est Nous qui resterons après la disparition de toutes les créatures. Nous hériterons de la Terre et tout ce qu’elle contient puisqu’ils laisseront tout derrière eux après leur disparition et de plus, Nous les possédons et disposons d’eux selon Notre bon vouloir. C’est à Nous Seul qu’ils retourneront le Jour de la Résurrection afin de rendre des comptes et être rétribués.","explicationEn":"40. I am the one who will remain after the creation has perished. I shall inherit the earth and those on it, because they will have perished and I will remain after them, and I own them and do with them as I want. To Me alone they shall return on the Day of Judgment to be reckoned and recompensed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ  إِنَّهُ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et mentionne dans le Livre, Abraham. C'était un très véridique et un Prophète.","tradEn":"And mention in the Book [the story of] Abraham. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, mentionne dans le Coran qui t’es révélé le récit d’Abraham. C’était un homme très véridique qui croyait de tout son être aux signes d’Allah et un prophète envoyé par Lui.","explicationEn":"41. And mention, O Messenger, in the Qur’ān which has been revealed to you the story of Abraham (peace be upon him). He was very truthful and firmly believed the signs of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ يَا أَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَلَا يُغْنِي عَنْكَ شَيْئًا","tradPropre":"Lorsqu'il dit à son père: «O mon père, pourquoi adores-tu ce qui n'entend ni ne voit, et ne te profite en rien?","tradEn":"[Mention] when he said to his father, \"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear and does not see and will not benefit you at all?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il dit à son père Âzar: Ô mon père, pourquoi adores-tu à la place d’Allah des idoles qui ne t’entendent pas lorsque tu les invoques ni ne te voient lorsque tu les adores? Pourquoi adorer ces idoles qui n’éloignent de toi aucun mal, ni ne te sont utiles?","explicationEn":"42. When he said to his father Azar: “O father, why do you worship besides Allah an idol which does not hear your supplication if you supplicate it, does not see your worship when you worship it, does not remove harm from you and does not bring any benefit to you?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي قَدْ جَاءَنِي مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَأْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِي أَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا","tradPropre":"O mon père, il m'est venu de la science ce que tu n'as pas reçu; suis-moi, donc, je te guiderai sur une voie droite.","tradEn":"O my father, indeed there has come to me of knowledge that which has not come to you, so follow me; I will guide you to an even path.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon père, je dispose d’une science qui m’a été révélée alors que tu n’en disposes pas. Suis-moi donc afin que je t’oriente vers le droit chemin.","explicationEn":"43. O father, such knowledge has come to me through revelation which has not come to you, so follow me and I shall guide you to the straight path.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"يَا أَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطَانَ  إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمَانِ عَصِيًّا","tradPropre":"O mon père, n'adore pas le Diable, car le Diable désobéit au Tout Miséricordieux.","tradEn":"O my father, do not worship [i.e., obey] Satan. Indeed Satan has ever been, to the Most Merciful, disobedient.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon père, ne sois pas un adorateur de Satan en lui obéissant car Satan a désobéi à Allah lorsqu’Il lui a ordonné de se prosterner à Adam.","explicationEn":"44. O father, do not worship the satan by obeying him. The satan is disobedient to the Merciful, as He ordered him to prostrate to Adam but he did not prostrate.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي أَخَافُ أَنْ يَمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِنَ الرَّحْمَانِ فَتَكُونَ لِلشَّيْطَانِ وَلِيًّا","tradPropre":"O mon père, je crains qu'un châtiment venant du Tout Miséricordieux ne te touche et que tu ne deviennes un allié du Diable».","tradEn":"O my father, indeed I fear that there will touch you a punishment from the Most Merciful so you would be to Satan a companion [in Hellfire].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô mon père, je crains que le Tout-Miséricordieux ne te châtie si tu mourrais mécréant. Tu deviendrais alors le partenaire de Satan dans le châtiment pour t’être allié à lui.","explicationEn":"45. O father, I fear a punishment from the Merciful will afflict you if you die in your disbelief, then you will be a companion to him in punishment due to your befriending him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَرَاغِبٌ أَنْتَ عَنْ آلِهَتِي يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ  لَئِنْ لَمْ تَنْتَهِ لَأَرْجُمَنَّكَ  وَاهْجُرْنِي مَلِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il dit: «O Abraham, aurais-tu du dédain pour mes divinités? Si tu ne cesses pas, certes je te lapiderai, éloigne-toi de moi pour bien longtemps».","tradEn":"[His father] said, \"Have you no desire for my gods, O Abraham? If you do not desist, I will surely stone you, so avoid me a prolonged time.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Âzar dit alors à son fils: Dédaignes-tu adorer les idoles que j’adore, ô Abraham? Si tu n’arrêtes pas de les insulter, je te lapiderai. Eloigne-toi de moi maintenant pour très longtemps: ne me parle plus et ne me fréquente plus.","explicationEn":"46. Azar said to his son Abraham (peace be upon him): “Are you turning away from the idols I worship, O Abraham? If you do not stop criticising my idols, I shall pelt you with stones. Leave me for a long time. Do not talk to me or be with me”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"قَالَ سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكَ  سَأَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّي  إِنَّهُ كَانَ بِي حَفِيًّا","tradPropre":"«Paix sur toi», dit Abraham. «J'implorerai mon Seigneur de te pardonner car Il m'a toujours comblé de Ses bienfaits.","tradEn":"[Abraham] said, \"Peace [i.e., safety] will be upon you. I will ask forgiveness for you of my Lord. Indeed, He is ever gracious to me.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Abraham répondit à son père: Paix sur toi de ma part. Tu ne subiras aucun mal venant de moi et je demanderai à mon Seigneur qu’Il te pardonne et te guide, car Il a toujours été indulgent avec moi.","explicationEn":"47. Abraham (peace be upon him) said to his father: “Greetings of peace to you from me. You will not face from me what you dislike. I shall seek forgiveness and guidance from my Lord for you. He is very kind to me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"وَأَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُونَ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَأَدْعُو رَبِّي عَسَىٰ أَلَّا أَكُونَ بِدُعَاءِ رَبِّي شَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"Je me sépare de vous, ainsi que de ce que vous invoquez, en dehors d'Allah, et j'invoquerai mon Seigneur. J'espère ne pas être malheureux dans mon appel à mon Seigneur».","tradEn":"And I will leave you and those you invoke other than Allāh and will invoke my Lord. I expect that I will not be in invocation to my Lord unhappy [i.e., disappointed].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Je m’en vais et délaisse les divinités que vous adorez à la place d’Allah et j’invoquerai Allah Seul sans Lui attribuer d’associé. J’espère qu’Il ne refusera pas de m’exaucer car son refus me rendrait malheureux.","explicationEn":"48. And I shall leave you and leave the idols you worship besides Allah, and I shall call upon my Lord alone, without associating any partner with Him. Perhaps He will not deprive me if I pray to Him, otherwise I will be unsuccessful in praying to Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُونَ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَهَبْنَا لَهُ إِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ  وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Puis, lorsqu'il se fut séparé d'eux et de ce qu'ils adoraient en dehors d'Allah, Nous lui fîmes don d'Isaac et de Jacob; et de chacun Nous fîmes un prophète.","tradEn":"So when he had left them and those they worshipped other than Allāh, We gave him Isaac and Jacob, and each [of them] We made a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Après être parti et avoir délaissé les idoles qu’ils adoraient au lieu d’adorer Allah, Nous l’avons dédommagé de la perte de sa famille en lui faisant le don d’un fils nommé Isaac puis d’un petit-fils nommé Jacob (Ya’qûb) et Nous avons fait de chacun d’eux des prophètes","explicationEn":"49. So when he left them and their gods they used to worship besides Allah, I replaced for him his loss of family, and so I gave him his son Isaac and I gave him his grandson Jacob. And each one of them I made a prophet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُمْ مِنْ رَحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et Nous leur donnâmes de par Notre miséricorde, et Nous leur accordâmes un langage sublime de vérité.","tradEn":"And We gave them of Our mercy, and We made for them a mention [i.e., reputation] of high honor.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Puisque juifs, chrétiens et musulmans célèbrent leurs mérites jusqu’à ce jour.","explicationUnanime":"Par miséricorde de notre part, Nous leur avons octroyé un immense bien en plus de la Prophétie et Nous avons fait en sorte que les gens fassent constamment leur éloge.","explicationEn":"50. And out of My mercy, I gave them much good alongside prophethood. And I established for them good praise which remains on the tongues of people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ مُوسَىٰ  إِنَّهُ كَانَ مُخْلَصًا وَكَانَ رَسُولًا نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et mentionne dans le Livre Moïse. C'était vraiment un élu, et c'était un Messager et un prophète.","tradEn":"And mention in the Book, Moses. Indeed, he was chosen, and he was a messenger and a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, mentionne dans le Coran qui t’a été révélé le récit de Moïse. C’était un homme élu ainsi qu’un messager et un prophète.","explicationEn":"51. And mention, O Messenger, in the Qur’ān revealed to you the story of Moses (peace be upon him). He was chosen and selected, and he was a Messenger and prophet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"وَنَادَيْنَاهُ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّورِ الْأَيْمَنِ وَقَرَّبْنَاهُ نَجِيًّا","tradPropre":"Du côté droit du Mont (Sinaï) Nous l'appelâmes et Nous le fîmes approcher tel un confident.","tradEn":"And We called him from the side of the mount at [his] right and brought him near, confiding [to him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous l’appelâmes du versant droit –par rapport au côté où se trouvait Moïse– de la montagne et Nous lui commandâmes d’approcher afin qu’il écoute ce qu’Allah avait à lui dire.","explicationEn":"52. I called him from the side of the mountain that was on the right in relation to where Moses (peace be upon him) was, and I brought him near in communion, where Allah let him hear His speech.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"وَوَهَبْنَا لَهُ مِنْ رَحْمَتِنَا أَخَاهُ هَارُونَ نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et par Notre miséricorde, Nous lui donnâmes Aaron son frère comme prophète.","tradEn":"And We gave him out of Our mercy his brother Aaron as a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Par Notre miséricorde et Notre bienfaisance, Nous avons exaucé son invocation et fait de son frère Aaron un prophète.","explicationEn":"53. I gave him, out of My grace and favour, his brother Aaron (peace be upon him) as a prophet, in answer to his prayer when he asked his Lord for that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِسْمَاعِيلَ  إِنَّهُ كَانَ صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ وَكَانَ رَسُولًا نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et mentionne Ismaël, dans le Livre. Il était fidèle à ses promesses; et c'était un Messager et un prophète.","tradEn":"And mention in the Book, Ishmael. Indeed, he was true to his promise, and he was a messenger and a prophet.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, mentionne dans le Coran qui t’a été révélé, le récit d’Ismaël. Il tenait chacune de ses promesses, et était un messager et un prophète.","explicationEn":"54. And mention, O Messenger, in the Qur’ān revealed to you, the story of Ishmael (peace be upon him). He was true to his promise - whenever he made a promise he fulfilled it - and he was a messenger and prophet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"وَكَانَ يَأْمُرُ أَهْلَهُ بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ وَكَانَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِ مَرْضِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et il commandait à sa famille la prière et la Zakât; et il était agréé auprès de son Seigneur.","tradEn":"And he used to enjoin on his people prayer and zakāh and was to his Lord pleasing [i.e., accepted by Him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ordonnait à sa famille d’accomplir la prière, de s’acquitter de l’aumône légale et était agréé auprès de son Seigneur.","explicationEn":"55. He used to instruct his household to keep up the prayer and to give Zakat, and his Lord was well pleased with him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ إِدْرِيسَ  إِنَّهُ كَانَ صِدِّيقًا نَبِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et mentionne Idris, dans le Livre. C'était un véridique et un prophète.","tradEn":"And mention in the Book, Idrees. Indeed, he was a man of truth and a prophet.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qui pourrait être l’Enoch de la Bible.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, mentionne dans le Coran qui t’a été révélé, le récit dIdrîs. Il était véridique, croyait de tout son être aux signes de son Seigneur en plus d’être un prophète envoyé par Allah.","explicationEn":"56. And mention, O Messenger, in the Qur’ān which has been revealed to you, the story of Idris (peace be upon him). He was very truthful and firmly believed in the signs of his Lord, and he was one of the prophets of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"وَرَفَعْنَاهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et Nous l'élevâmes à un haut rang.","tradEn":"And We raised him to a high station.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Les termes employés peuvent également signifier qu’il fut élevé au Ciel, comme le relate la Bible (Genèse 5, 24).","explicationUnanime":"La Prophétie que Nous lui avons octroyée éleva sa mention et son rang.","explicationEn":"57. I raised his mention by the prophethood I gave him and he therefore was of a high rank.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"أُولَائِكَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنَ النَّبِيِّينَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ آدَمَ وَمِمَّنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوحٍ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْرَائِيلَ وَمِمَّنْ هَدَيْنَا وَاجْتَبَيْنَا  إِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ آيَاتُ الرَّحْمَانِ خَرُّوا سُجَّدًا وَبُكِيًّا ۩","tradPropre":"Voilà ceux qu'Allah a comblés de faveurs, parmi les prophètes, parmi les descendants d'Adam, et aussi parmi ceux que Nous avons transportés en compagnie de Noé, et parmi la descendance d'Abraham et d'Israël, et parmi ceux que Nous avons guidés et choisis. Quand les versets du Tout Miséricordieux leur étaient récités, ils tombaient prosternés en pleurant.","tradEn":"Those were the ones upon whom Allāh bestowed favor from among the prophets of the descendants of Adam and of those We carried [in the ship] with Noah, and of the descendants of Abraham and Israel [i.e., Jacob], and of those whom We guided and chose. When the verses of the Most Merciful were recited to them, they fell in prostration and weeping.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les hommes mentionnés précédemment dans cette sourate, à commencer par Zacharie jusqu’à Idrîs sont ceux à qui Allah a octroyé le bienfait de la Prophétie parmi les descendants d’Adam, les descendants de ceux que Nous avons embarqué dans l’Arche en compagnie de Noé et les descendants d’Abraham et de Jacob. Ce sont aussi ceux à qui Nous avons facilité la guidée à l’Islam. Nous les avons élus et avons fait d’eux des prophètes qui, lorsqu’ils entendaient les versets d’Allah être récités, se prosternaient en pleurant de crainte.","explicationEn":"58. Those who were mentioned in this Sūrah, beginning with Zachariah and ending with Idris (peace be upon them) are the ones whom Allah blessed with prophethood, from the children of Adam (peace be upon him), and from the children of those whom I carried in the Ark with Noah (peace be upon him), and from the children of Abraham and the children of Jacob (peace be upon them), and from those whom I blessed with guidance to Islam and whom I chose and made prophets. When they heard the verses of Allah being recited, they prostrated to Allah, weeping out of His fear.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"۞ فَخَلَفَ مِنْ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ أَضَاعُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوَاتِ  فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا","tradPropre":"Puis leur succédèrent des générations qui délaissèrent la prière et suivirent leurs passions. Ils se trouveront en perdition,","tradEn":"But there came after them successors [i.e., later generations] who neglected prayer and pursued desires; so they are going to meet evil -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"A ces prophètes élus succédèrent des générations égarées qui ont délaissé la prière en ne l’accomplissant plus comme il faut et ont commis les actes de désobéissance que leurs âmes leur commandaient, comme la fornication par exemple. Ils seront maudits en Enfer et rétribués pour le mal qu’ils ont accompli.","explicationEn":"59. After these chosen prophets came followers of evil and deviation, who neglected prayer by not offering it in the required manner, and who perpetrated sins driven by their own desires such as fornication. These people will come face to face with evil and disappointment in Hell.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَآمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَأُولَائِكَ يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُونَ شَيْئًا","tradPropre":"sauf celui qui se repent, croit et fait le bien: ceux-là entreront dans le Paradis et ne seront point lésés,","tradEn":"Except those who repent, believe and do righteousness; for those will enter Paradise and will not be wronged at all.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il sera fait exception de ceux qui se seront repentis de leurs manquements, auront cru en Allah et accompli de bonnes œuvres. Ceux-là, Nous les ferons entrer au Paradis et rien ne manquera à la rétribution que Nous leur remettrons, pas même une part négligeable.","explicationEn":"60. But those who repented from their neglect and excess, who had faith in Allah, and who did righteous deeds; those who possess such attributes will enter Paradise and the reward of their actions will not be reduced in the least.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ الَّتِي وَعَدَ الرَّحْمَانُ عِبَادَهُ بِالْغَيْبِ  إِنَّهُ كَانَ وَعْدُهُ مَأْتِيًّا","tradPropre":"aux jardins du séjour (éternel) que le Tout Miséricordieux a promis à Ses serviteurs, [qui ont cru] au mystère. Car Sa promesse arrivera sans nul doute.","tradEn":"[Therein are] gardens of perpetual residence which the Most Merciful has promised His servants in the unseen. Indeed, His promise has ever been eminent.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils demeureront éternellement dans les jardins que le Tout-Miséricordieux a promis à Ses serviteurs vertueux qui ont cru en cette promesse alors qu’ils n’avaient jamais vu le Paradis. Ainsi, même si on ne voit pas le Paradis, la promesse d’y entrer est certainement véridique.","explicationEn":"61. Gardens of residence and permanence, which the Merciful promised His servants in the Ghaib that He will make them enter them. They did not see them but they believed in them. Allah’s promise of Paradise - even though it is in the Ghaib - will most certainly come to pass.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"لَا يَسْمَعُونَ فِيهَا لَغْوًا إِلَّا سَلَامًا  وَلَهُمْ رِزْقُهُمْ فِيهَا بُكْرَةً وَعَشِيًّا","tradPropre":"On n'y entend nulle parole insignifiante; seulement: «Salâm»; et ils auront là leur nourriture, matin et soir.","tradEn":"They will not hear therein any ill speech - only [greetings of] peace - and they will have their provision therein, morning and afternoon.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils n’y entendront aucune parole frivole ni obscène. Ils y entendront plutôt leurs paroles mutuelles et le salut des anges. En outre, ils y recevront la nourriture qu’ils désirent matin et soir.","explicationEn":"62. There they will not hear anything futile nor any obscene talk. Instead they will hear the greeting of peace to one another and the greeting of peace from the angels to them. They will be given whatever type of food they desire in the morning and evening.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"تِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِي نُورِثُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا مَنْ كَانَ تَقِيًّا","tradPropre":"Voilà le Paradis dont Nous ferons hériter ceux de Nos serviteurs qui auront été pieux.","tradEn":"That is Paradise, which We give as inheritance to those of Our servants who were fearing of Allāh.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Paradis décrit ici est ce dont Nous ferons don à Nos serviteurs qui se conformaient à Nos commandements et délaissaient Nos interdits. Puis après avoir mentionné la récompense des serviteurs pieux,","explicationEn":"63. This Paradise, described with the above attributes, is the one that I will give to those of My servants who fulfilled the Commandments and avoided the Prohibitions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"وَمَا نَتَنَزَّلُ إِلَّا بِأَمْرِ رَبِّكَ  لَهُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِينَا وَمَا خَلْفَنَا وَمَا بَيْنَ ذَالِكَ  وَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ نَسِيًّا","tradPropre":"«Nous ne descendons que sur ordre de ton Seigneur. A Lui tout ce qui est devant nous, tout ce qui est derrière nous et tout ce qui est entre les deux. Ton Seigneur n'oublie rien.","tradEn":"[Gabriel said], \"And we [angels] descend not except by the order of your Lord. To Him belongs that before us and that behind us and what is in between. And never is your Lord forgetful -","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : de l’au-delà, de ce bas monde et du monde intermédiaire.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Gabriel, dis à Muħammad: Les anges ne descendent pas de leur propre chef mais plutôt par ordre d’Allah. C’est à Allah qu’appartient la connaissance de ce qui aura lieu dans l’au-delà, de ce que nous avons laissé dans le bas monde et de ce qui a lieu entre le bas monde et l’au-delà. Ô Messager, il n’est pas concevable que ton Seigneur oublie quoi que ce soit.","explicationEn":"64. And say - O Gabriel - to Muhammad (peace be upon him): The angels do not descent of their own accord. They only descend at Allah’s command. Everything ahead of us in the Hearafter, everything behind us in the world, and everything in between the world and the Hearafter, all belong to Allah. Your Lord, O Messenger, would not forget anything.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فَاعْبُدْهُ وَاصْطَبِرْ لِعِبَادَتِهِ  هَلْ تَعْلَمُ لَهُ سَمِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il est le Seigneur des cieux et de la terre et de tout ce qui est entre eux. Adore-Le donc, et sois constant dans Son adoration. Lui connais-tu un homonyme?»","tradEn":"Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them - so worship Him and have patience for His worship. Do you know of any similarity to Him?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il est le Créateur des Cieux et de la Terre, leur Possesseur et leur Gestionnaire. Il est également le Créateur, le Possesseur et le Gestionnaire de ce qui se trouve entre les deux. Adore-Le donc Seul, puisqu’Il mérite d’être adoré, et soit constant dans ton adoration, car Il n’a aucun semblable pouvant prétendre être adoré avec Lui.","explicationEn":"65. He is the Creator of the heavens and the Creator of the earth and their Owner and Controller. He is also the Creator, Owner and Controller of everything in between them so worship Him alone, for He alone is deserving of worship. Remain firm in worshipping Him, for He has no likeness or partner who shares this worship with Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"وَيَقُولُ الْإِنْسَانُ أَإِذَا مَا مِتُّ لَسَوْفَ أُخْرَجُ حَيًّا","tradPropre":"Et l'homme dit: «Une fois mort, me sortira-t-on vivant?»","tradEn":"And man [i.e., the disbeliever] says, \"When I have died, am I going to be brought forth alive?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le mécréant qui rejette la réalité de la Ressuscitation dit sur un ton moqueur: Serai-je extrait de ma tombe après ma mort pour vivre une seconde vie? Ceci est certainement impossible.","explicationEn":"66. The disbeliever, who rejects resurrection, mockingly says: What, when I die, I will come out of my grave alive for a second time? This is far-fetched.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"أَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْإِنْسَانُ أَنَّا خَلَقْنَاهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا","tradPropre":"L'homme ne se rappelle-t-il pas qu'avant cela, c'est Nous qui l'avons créé, alors qu'il n'était rien?","tradEn":"Does man not remember that We created him before, while he was nothing?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce dénégateur ne se rappelle-t-il pas que Nous l’avons créé auparavant à partir du néant. On prouve donc la réalité de la seconde création par la première qui est évidente, sachant que la seconde est plus facile et plus aisée à accomplir que la première.","explicationEn":"67. Does this person who rejects resurrection not remember that I created him previously when he was nothing? He can then use the first creation as evidence for the second creation, even though the second creation will be simpler and easier?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"فَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحْشُرَنَّهُمْ وَالشَّيَاطِينَ ثُمَّ لَنُحْضِرَنَّهُمْ حَوْلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيًّا","tradPropre":"Par ton Seigneur! Assurément, Nous les rassemblerons, eux et les diables. Puis, Nous les placerons autour de l'Enfer, agenouillés.","tradEn":"So by your Lord, We will surely gather them and the devils; then We will bring them to be present around Hell upon their knees.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Par ton Seigneur, ô Messager, Nous les sortirons de leurs tombes et les rassemblerons en compagnie des démons qui les ont égarés, puis Nous les conduirons agenouillés et avilis vers les portes de l’Enfer.","explicationEn":"68. By your Lord, O Messenger, I will take them out of their graves to the place of gathering along with the satans who had misled them. Then I will push them towards the doors of Hell, humiliated and on their knees.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ لَنَنْزِعَنَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شِيعَةٍ أَيُّهُمْ أَشَدُّ عَلَى الرَّحْمَانِ عِتِيًّا","tradPropre":"Ensuite, Nous arracherons de chaque groupe ceux d'entre eux qui étaient les plus obstinés contre le Tout Miséricordieux.","tradEn":"Then We will surely extract from every sect those of them who were worst against the Most Merciful in insolence.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qui seront châtiés en premier, expliquent certains exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Puis Nous extrairons violemment de chaque secte égarée les plus désobéissants de leurs membres. Il s’agit des meneurs de ces sectes.","explicationEn":"69. I shall violently pull out from each of the groups of deviation those who were most disobedient, and these are their leaders.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ لَنَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِالَّذِينَ هُمْ أَوْلَىٰ بِهَا صِلِيًّا","tradPropre":"Puis nous sommes Le meilleur à savoir ceux qui méritent le plus d'y être brûlés.","tradEn":"Then, surely it is We who are most knowing of those most worthy of burning therein.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous serons alors les plus à même de connaître ceux qui méritent le plus d’entrer dans le Feu et d’endurer sa chaleur.","explicationEn":"70. Then I know best about those who most deserve to enter the Fire and endure and suffer its heat.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَا  كَانَ عَلَىٰ رَبِّكَ حَتْمًا مَقْضِيًّا","tradPropre":"Il n'y a personne parmi vous qui ne passera pas par [L'Enfer]: Car [il s'agit là] pour ton Seigneur d'une sentence irrévocable.","tradEn":"And there is none of you except he will come to it. This is upon your Lord an inevitability decreed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, chacun de vous devra traverser le Pont qui surplombe l’Enfer. Cette traversée a été décrétée par Allah et est irrévocable.","explicationEn":"71. There is not one among you - O people - who will not cross over the bridge placed over Hell. Your Lord has made this crossing an incumbent decree and no one can push back His decree.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَنَذَرُ الظَّالِمِينَ فِيهَا جِثِيًّا","tradPropre":"Ensuite, Nous délivrerons ceux qui étaient pieux et Nous y laisserons les injustes agenouillés.","tradEn":"Then We will save those who feared Allāh and leave the wrongdoers within it, on their knees.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Selon certains exégètes, le pronom « vous » au verset précédent désigne uniquement les impies qui entreront tous en Enfer, tandis que les croyants seront sauvés. Selon d’autres, ces paroles s’adressent également aux croyants qui, soit entreront en Enfer momentanément, mais sans en subir les affres, soit s’en approcheront seulement sans y entrer, soit traverseront le Pont qui enjambe l’Enfer, mais sans y tomber, contrairement aux mécréants.","explicationUnanime":"Après cela, Nous accorderons le salut à ceux qui craignaient leur Seigneur par leur observance de Ses commandements et le renoncement à Ses interdits, et laisserons les injustes agenouillés sans qu’on ne leur permette de changer de position.","explicationEn":"72. Then after this crossing over the bridge, I will deliver those who were mindful of their Lord by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions, and I will leave the wrongdoers kneeling on their knees without being able to escape from it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"وَإِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ آيَاتُنَا بَيِّنَاتٍ قَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَيُّ الْفَرِيقَيْنِ خَيْرٌ مَقَامًا وَأَحْسَنُ نَدِيًّا","tradPropre":"Et lorsque Nos versets évidents leur sont récités les mécréants disent à ceux qui croient: «Lequel des deux groupes a la situation la plus confortable et la meilleure compagnie?»","tradEn":"And when Our verses are recited to them as clear evidences, those who disbelieve say to those who believe, \"Which of [our] two parties is best in position and best in association?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque Nos versets clairs révélés à Notre Messager sont récités aux gens, les mécréants disent aux croyants: Qui de nos deux camps jouit du meilleur confort et de la meilleure compagnie: le nôtre ou le vôtre?","explicationEn":"73. When My clear revelations to My Messenger are recited to people, the disbelievers say to the believers: Which of our two parties is better in residence and dwelling and superior in assembly and gathering: Our party or your party?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"وَكَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ أَحْسَنُ أَثَاثًا وَرِئْيًا","tradPropre":"Combien de générations, avant eux, avons-Nous fait périr, qui les surpassaient en biens et en apparence?","tradEn":"And how many a generation have We destroyed before them who were better in possessions and [outward] appearance?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Qu’ils sont nombreux les peuples que Nous avons anéantis bien avant ces mécréants qui s’enorgueillissent de leur supériorité matérielle. Ces peuples les surpassaient en richesse, en belle apparence et en corpulence.","explicationEn":"74. How many were the nations that I destroyed before these disbelievers who are proud of their material superiority, who had surpassed them in riches and in their outward appearance due to their expensive clothing and their bodily luxuries.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"قُلْ مَنْ كَانَ فِي الضَّلَالَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ لَهُ الرَّحْمَانُ مَدًّا  حَتَّىٰ إِذَا رَأَوْا مَا يُوعَدُونَ إِمَّا الْعَذَابَ وَإِمَّا السَّاعَةَ فَسَيَعْلَمُونَ مَنْ هُوَ شَرٌّ مَكَانًا وَأَضْعَفُ جُنْدًا","tradPropre":"Dis: «Celui qui est dans l'égarement, que le Tout Miséricordieux prolonge sa vie pour un certain temps, jusqu'à ce qu'ils voient soit le châtiment, soit l'Heure dont ils sont menacés. Alors, ils sauront qui a la pire situation et la troupe la plus faible».","tradEn":"Say, \"Whoever is in error - let the Most Merciful extend for him an extension [in wealth and time] until, when they see that which they were promised - either punishment [in this world] or the Hour [of resurrection] - they will come to know who is worst in position and weaker in soldiers.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ceux qui débattent dans leur égarement que le Tout-Miséricordieux leur accordera un répit afin que leur égarement empire et lorsqu’ils verront le châtiment qu’ils subiront dans le bas monde ou dans l’au-delà, ils sauront alors qui est celui qui a la pire la position et qui a le moins de soutien. Est-ce leur camp ou celui des croyants?","explicationEn":"75. Say - O Messenger: The Merciful will grant respite to those wallowing in their misguidance, so that they fall further into it, until when they see what they have been warned about- either the swift punishment in this world or the punishment postponed to the Day of Judgment - then they will realise who is worse situated and who has the weakest forces. Is it their party or the party of the believers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"وَيَزِيدُ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ اهْتَدَوْا هُدًى  وَالْبَاقِيَاتُ الصَّالِحَاتُ خَيْرٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابًا وَخَيْرٌ مَرَدًّا","tradPropre":"Allah accroît la rectitude de ceux qui suivent le bon chemin, et les bonnes œuvres durables méritent auprès de ton Seigneur une meilleure récompense et une meilleure destination.","tradEn":"And Allāh increases those who were guided, in guidance, and the enduring good deeds are better to your Lord for reward and better for recourse.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis qu’Il accordera un répit aux mécréants afin qu’ils s’égarent plus encore, Il fera accroître la foi et l’obéissance des croyants et multiplier les bonnes œuvres qui les mèneront au bonheur éternel. Ô Messager, ceci est une rétribution de ton Seigneur plus utile au serviteur qui lui permettra d’aller vers une fin plus heureuse.","explicationEn":"76. In contrast to the respite granted to those people so that they fall further into misguidance, Allah gives more guidance and obedience to those who are guided. Righteous deeds that lead to perpetual happiness are more beneficial - in the sight of your Lord, O messenger, in terms of their recompense and have a better outcome.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"أَفَرَأَيْتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ بِآيَاتِنَا وَقَالَ لَأُوتَيَنَّ مَالًا وَوَلَدًا","tradPropre":"As-tu vu celui qui ne croit pas à Nos versets et dit: «On me donnera certes des biens et des enfants»?","tradEn":"Then, have you seen he who disbelieved in Our verses and said, \"I will surely be given wealth and children [in the next life]\"?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, as-tu vu celui qui n’accorde aucun crédit à Nos arguments et rejette Notre avertissement? Il dit en effet: Lorsque je mourrai et serai ressuscité, on m’octroiera de grandes richesses et une descendance nombreuse.","explicationEn":"77. Have you, O messenger, seen the man who denies My evidences, rejects My warning and says: If I die and am resurrected, I will certainly be given a lot of wealth and children?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"أَطَّلَعَ الْغَيْبَ أَمِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمَانِ عَهْدًا","tradPropre":"Est-il au courant de l'Inconnaissable ou a-t-il pris un engagement avec le Tout Miséricordieux?","tradEn":"Has he looked into the unseen, or has he taken from the Most Merciful a promise?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Est-il au fait de l’Invisible lorsqu’il dit cela ou s’appuie-t-il sur une preuve tangible? Ou encore, a-t-il obtenu l’engagement d’Allah de le faire entrer en Paradis et de lui accorder ce qu’il prétend?","explicationEn":"78. Does he have knowledge of the Ghaib and therefore he said that with some proof? Or does he have a pledge with his Lord to enter him into paradise and to give him wealth and children?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا  سَنَكْتُبُ مَا يَقُولُ وَنَمُدُّ لَهُ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ مَدًّا","tradPropre":"Bien au contraire! Nous enregistrerons ce qu'il dit et accroîtrons son châtiment.","tradEn":"No! We will record what he says and extend [i.e., increase] for him from the punishment extensively.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce n’est pas le cas, contrairement à ses allégations. Nous consignerons ses paroles et ses agissements et dédoublerons son châtiment pour ses allégations mensongères.","explicationEn":"79. The matter is not as he claimed. I will certainly record what he says and does; and I will give him a punishment over and above his punishment because of the falsehood that he claims.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"وَنَرِثُهُ مَا يَقُولُ وَيَأْتِينَا فَرْدًا","tradPropre":"C'est Nous qui hériterons ce dont il parle, tandis qu'il viendra à Nous, tout seul.","tradEn":"And We will inherit him [in] what he mentions, and he will come to Us alone.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous récupèrerons alors les biens et la descendance qu’il a laissés après l’avoir anéanti et il viendra à Nous seul le Jour de la Résurrection, dépourvu de la richesse et du prestige qui faisaient sa force dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"80. I shall inherit the wealth and children he leaves behind after I destroy him, and he will come to Us on the Day of Judgement all alone, with the wealth and fame that he enjoyed having been taken away from him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"وَاتَّخَذُوا مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ آلِهَةً لِيَكُونُوا لَهُمْ عِزًّا","tradPropre":"Ils ont adopté des divinités en dehors d'Allah pour qu'ils leur soient des protecteurs (contre le châtiment).","tradEn":"And they have taken besides Allāh [false] deities that they would be for them [a source of] honor.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les polythéistes ont adopté des divinités à la place d’Allah afin qu’ils les secourent et les assistent.","explicationEn":"81. The idolaters have taken for themselves things of worship other than Allah, so that they may be a support and source of assistance for them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا  سَيَكْفُرُونَ بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ وَيَكُونُونَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضِدًّا","tradPropre":"Bien au contraire! [ces divinités] renieront leur adoration et seront pour eux des adversaires.","tradEn":"No! They [i.e., those \"gods\"] will deny their worship of them and will be against them opponents [on the Day of Judgement].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : il n’en sera rien. Ces divinités renieront au contraire leur adoration et leur déclareront leur animosité.","explicationUnanime":"Or le Jour de la Résurrection, ces divinités renieront l’adoration que leur vouaient les polythéistes, les désavoueront et se feront leurs ennemis.","explicationEn":"82. The matter is not as they claimed. These things that they worshipped besides Allah will reject the idolaters’ worship of them on the Day of Judgment. They will disassociate themselves from them and become their enemies.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّا أَرْسَلْنَا الشَّيَاطِينَ عَلَى الْكَافِرِينَ تَؤُزُّهُمْ أَزًّا","tradPropre":"N'as-tu pas vu que Nous avons envoyé contre les mécréants des diables qui les excitent furieusement [à désobéir]?","tradEn":"Do you not see that We have sent the devils upon the disbelievers, inciting them [to evil] with [constant] incitement?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, n’as-tu pas vu que Nous avons envoyé les démons et que Nous leur avons accordé une emprise sur les mécréants, les incitant à commettre des actes de désobéissance et à détourner les gens de la religion d’Allah?","explicationEn":"83. Have you, O Messenger, not seen that I sent the satans and gave them authority over the disbelievers inciting them to commit sins and prevent others from Allah’s religion?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"فَلَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ  إِنَّمَا نَعُدُّ لَهُمْ عَدًّا","tradPropre":"Ne te hâte donc pas contre eux: Nous tenons un compte précis de [tous leurs actes].","tradEn":"So be not impatient over them. We only count out [i.e., allow] to them a [limited] number.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ne t’empresse pas de demander à Allah de hâter leur anéantissement car Nous connaissons avec précision les durées de leurs vies et lorsque le répit que Nous leur accordons se termine, Nous les punissons de la manière qu’ils méritent.","explicationEn":"84. Do not be hasty, O Messenger, in asking Allah to punish them quickly. I am keeping a close record of their lives, until when the period of their respite comes to an end, I will punish them with what they deserve.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"يَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ الْمُتَّقِينَ إِلَى الرَّحْمَانِ وَفْدًا","tradPropre":"(Rappelle-toi) le jour où Nous rassemblerons les pieux sur des montures et en grande pompe, auprès du Tout Miséricordieux,","tradEn":"On the Day We will gather the righteous to the Most Merciful as a delegation","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi que le Jour de la Résurrection, Nous rassemblerons ceux qui craignaient Allah, observaient Ses commandements et renonçaient à Ses interdits, et les mènerons auprès de leur Seigneur avec les honneurs.","explicationEn":"85. Remember, O Messenger, the Day of Judgment when I will gather those who were mindful of their Lord - by fulfilling His instructions and avoiding His prohibitions - to their Lord as a delegation that is honoured and respected.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"وَنَسُوقُ الْمُجْرِمِينَ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ وِرْدًا","tradPropre":"et pousserons les criminels à l'Enfer comme (un troupeau) à l'abreuvoir,","tradEn":"And will drive the criminals to Hell in thirst","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis que les mécréants seront conduits en Enfer dans un état de soif extrême.","explicationEn":"86. I will drive the disbelievers to Hell thirsty.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"لَا يَمْلِكُونَ الشَّفَاعَةَ إِلَّا مَنِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمَانِ عَهْدًا","tradPropre":"ils ne disposeront d'aucune intercession, sauf celui qui aura pris un engagement avec le Tout Miséricordieux.","tradEn":"None will have [power of] intercession except he who had taken from the Most Merciful a covenant.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Et ne pourront eux-mêmes intercéder en faveur des autres.","explicationUnanime":"Ces mécréants n’auront pas le pouvoir d’intercéder les uns en faveur des autres, excepté ceux qui se seront engagés auprès d’Allah dans le bas monde à croire en Lui et en Ses messagers.","explicationEn":"87. These disbelievers will not have the power to intercede for one another, except for those who had taken a pledge with Allah in the world by having faith in Him and in His messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمَانُ وَلَدًا","tradPropre":"Et ils ont dit: «Le Tout Miséricordieux S'est attribué un enfant!»","tradEn":"And they say, \"The Most Merciful has taken [for Himself] a son.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les juifs, les chrétiens et certains polythéistes prétendent qu’Allah s’est donné un fils.","explicationEn":"88. The Jews, the Christians and some of the idolaters said: The Merciful has taken a son.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"لَقَدْ جِئْتُمْ شَيْئًا إِدًّا","tradPropre":"Vous avancez certes là une chose abominable!","tradEn":"You have done an atrocious thing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô vous qui prétendez cela, vous dites là quelque chose d’affreux.","explicationEn":"89. You - who say this - have indeed brought something monstrous.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"تَكَادُ السَّمَاوَاتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْهُ وَتَنْشَقُّ الْأَرْضُ وَتَخِرُّ الْجِبَالُ هَدًّا","tradPropre":"Peu s'en faut que les cieux ne s'entrouvrent à ces mots, que la terre ne se fende et que les montagnes ne s'écroulent,","tradEn":"The heavens almost rupture therefrom and the earth splits open and the mountains collapse in devastation","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les Cieux et la Terre manquent de se fendre et les montagnes manquent de s’écrouler, à cause de ces paroles ignobles.","explicationEn":"90. The heavens almost rupture because of this detested statement, the earth almost splits, and the mountains almost fall in ruins.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"أَنْ دَعَوْا لِلرَّحْمَانِ وَلَدًا","tradPropre":"du fait qu'ils ont attribué un enfant au Tout Miséricordieux,","tradEn":"That they attribute to the Most Merciful a son.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces phénomènes sont dus à leur allégation selon laquelle Allah a un fils, qu’Il soit hautement élevé au-dessus de cette ignominie.","explicationEn":"91. All of this because they have attributed a son to the Merciful. Allah is high above that by far.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"وَمَا يَنْبَغِي لِلرَّحْمَانِ أَنْ يَتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا","tradPropre":"alors qu'il ne convient nullement au Tout Miséricordieux d'avoir un enfant!","tradEn":"And it is not appropriate for the Most Merciful that He should take a son.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ne convient pas que le Tout-Miséricordieux ait un enfant, cela est exclu.","explicationEn":"92. It is not befitting of the Merciful to take a son as He is pure of that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"إِنْ كُلُّ مَنْ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ إِلَّا آتِي الرَّحْمَانِ عَبْدًا","tradPropre":"Tous ceux qui sont dans les cieux et sur la terre se rendront auprès du Tout Miséricordieux, [sans exception], en serviteurs.","tradEn":"There is no one in the heavens and earth but that he comes to the Most Merciful as a servant.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Toutes les créatures présentes dans les Cieux et sur Terre –anges, humains et djinns– se rendront le Jour de la Résurrection, en toute soumission auprès de leur Seigneur.","explicationEn":"93. There is no angel, human being or jinn in the heavens and earth but that he will come in submission to his Lord on the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-94.html"},{"numVerset":94,"texteArabe":"لَقَدْ أَحْصَاهُمْ وَعَدَّهُمْ عَدًّا","tradPropre":"Il les a certes dénombrés et bien comptés.","tradEn":"He has enumerated them and counted them a [full] counting.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils les cernent tous de Sa connaissance, Lui qui les a tous dénombrés. Rien de ce qui les concerne ne Lui échappe donc.","explicationEn":"94. He has full knowledge of them and has numbered them exactly. Nothing of theirs is hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019094","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-93.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-95.html"},{"numVerset":95,"texteArabe":"وَكُلُّهُمْ آتِيهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فَرْدًا","tradPropre":"Et au Jour de la Résurrection, chacun d'eux se rendra seul auprès de Lui.","tradEn":"And all of them are coming to Him on the Day of Resurrection alone.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis le Jour de la Résurrection, chacun d’eux se rendra individuellement auprès de Lui sans être accompagné par sa richesse ou par un secoureur.","explicationEn":"95. Each one of them will come to Him on the Day of Judgment alone, without any helper or any wealth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019095","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-94.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-96.html"},{"numVerset":96,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ سَيَجْعَلُ لَهُمُ الرَّحْمَانُ وُدًّا","tradPropre":"A ceux qui croient et font de bonnes œuvres, le Tout Miséricordieux accordera Son amour.","tradEn":"Indeed, those who have believed and done righteous deeds - the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah accordera Son amour à ceux qui croient en Allah et accomplissent des œuvres qu’Il agrée et inspirera aux gens de les aimer.","explicationEn":"96. Those who have faith in Allah, and do righteous actions that Allah is pleased with, Allah will create for them love by His loving them and by making them beloved to His servants.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019096","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-95.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-97.html"},{"numVerset":97,"texteArabe":"فَإِنَّمَا يَسَّرْنَاهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لِتُبَشِّرَ بِهِ الْمُتَّقِينَ وَتُنْذِرَ بِهِ قَوْمًا لُدًّا","tradPropre":"Nous l'avons rendu (le Coran) facile [à comprendre] en ta langue, afin que tu annonces par lui la bonne nouvelle aux gens pieux, et que, tu avertisses un peuple irréductible.","tradEn":"So, [O Muḥammad], We have only made it [i.e., the Qur’ān] easy in your tongue [i.e., the Arabic language] that you may give good tidings thereby to the righteous and warn thereby a hostile people.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, Nous avons facilité la compréhension de Coran en te le révélant dans ta langue. Ceci, afin que tu annonces la bonne nouvelle aux pieux, qui observent Mes commandements et renoncent à Mes interdits, et que tu menaces des gens tenaces dans leur opposition et leur dédain de reconnaître la vérité.","explicationEn":"97. We have made this Qur’ān easy by revealing it in your own language, O Messenger, so that you may bring glad news to those who are mindful by fulfilling My instructions and avoiding My prohibitions, and so that you may warn a people who are harsh in disputing and stubborn in accepting the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019097","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-96.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-19-verset-98.html"},{"numVerset":98,"texteArabe":"وَكَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِنْ قَرْنٍ هَلْ تُحِسُّ مِنْهُمْ مِنْ أَحَدٍ أَوْ تَسْمَعُ لَهُمْ رِكْزًا","tradPropre":"Que de générations avant eux avons-Nous fait périr! En retrouves-tu un seul individu? ou en entends-tu le moindre murmure?","tradEn":"And how many have We destroyed before them of generations? Do you perceive of them anyone or hear from them a sound?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Qu’ils sont nombreux les peuples que Nous avons anéantis avant le tien! Connais-tu un seul représentant de ces peuples en vie ou entends-tu parler d’eux? Ce qui s’est abattu sur eux peut s’abattre sur d’autres si Allah le décide.","explicationEn":"98. How many communities I have destroyed before your people! Do you perceive a single one of those communities today, or hear any sound from them? What afflicted them may afflict others when Allah gives permission.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"019098","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-97.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-1.html"}]};